(2) [12 marks]
(a) State the following axioms for inequalities $\leq$ in $\mathbb{Z}$.

The axioms should include appropriate quantifiers.
Transitive (Tr)
$$\forall a, b, c \in \mathbb{Z} \quad a \leq b \wedge b \leq c \Rightarrow a \leq c$$

Shift (Sh)
$$\forall a, b, c \in \mathbb{Z} \quad a \leqslant b \Rightarrow a+c \leqslant b+c$$
(b) Prove the following statement:
$$\forall a, b, c, d \in \mathbb{Z} , \text { if } a \leq c \text { and } b \leq d \text { then } a+b \leq c+d .$$

You should justify each line of your proof, clearly indicating the premise and any axioms that you use (including the above axioms).

\section*{Proof:}
$$\begin{array}{ll}
a \leq c \text { and } b \leq d & \text { (premise) } \\
a+b \leq c+b & \text { (sh) from premise } \\
b+c \leq d+c & \text { (sh) from premise } \\
c+b \leq c+d & \text { (comm.) } \\
a+b \leq c+d & \text { (Tr) from lines 2,4. }
\end{array}$$
