(c) Prove by induction that for all $n \geq 1$
$$\sum_{k=1}^{n} 4 k^{3}=n^{2}(n+1)^{2}$$

You do not need to indicate which axioms you use at each step but you should indicate the logical steps of the proof by induction.

Base step: $n=1$
$$\begin{aligned}
& \sum_{k=1}^{n} 4 k^{3}=4 \cdot 1^{3}=4 \quad n^{2}(n+1)^{2}=1^{2} \cdot 2^{2}=4 \\
& \text { so } \sum_{k=1}^{n} 4 k^{3}=n^{2}(n+1)^{2}
\end{aligned}$$

Induction step: suppose that for
some n: $\sum_{k=1}^{n} 4 k^{3}=n^{2}(n+1)^{2} \quad \begin{gathered}(\text { induction } \\ \text { hyp). }\end{gathered}$
Then $\sum_{k=1}^{n+1} 4 k^{3}=\sum_{k=1}^{n} 4 k^{3}+4(n+1)^{3}\binom{\text { def of }}{\sum}$
$$\begin{aligned}
& =n^{2}(n+1)^{2}+4(n+1)^{3} \quad \text{(sub.)} \\
& =\left(n^{2}+4(n+1)\right) \cdot(n+1)^{2} \\
& =\left(n^{2}+4 n+4\right) \cdot(n+1)^{2} \\
& =(n+1)^{2}(n+2)^{2} .
\end{aligned}$$
so result holds for $n+1$.
Hence by induction $\sum_{k=1}^{n} 4 k^{3}=n^{2}(n+1)^{2}$
for all $n \geqslant 1$
